 Hierarchy uses registered canonical paths only. It does not scan for projects or resolve symlink aliases. Nesting does not change Session working directories, logs, or Workspace membership. Deleting a parent Workspace leaves its child Workspaces registered and places them under their next registered ancestor, or at the root.
 
+The Workspace edit dialog exposes the root-scoped `sidebar.workspaces.workspace.edit` slot. Its owner receives `WorkspaceEditOwnerProps { workspaceId: WorkspaceId; path: string; title: string }`, where `path` is the canonical primary Workspace path. A Client plugin can place additional source-folder controls there without renaming the Workspace or changing its primary path; choosing another file-browser root does not change Session cwd.
